# Runtime state, not source. The root .gitignore already draws this line for the
# journal ("your own trade history, not source"); these are the paper trader's
# equivalents and belong on the same side of it.

# The live paper portfolio: cash, open positions, equity curve. This is your
# trading state. Committing it means every session's positions land in the
# history, and a checkout on another machine would silently restore someone
# else's book.
data/paper_book.json

# Caches, rebuilt on demand. The liquidity cache is ~1 MB of scratch that exists
# only so a rate-limited screen can resume; the universe is re-screened weekly.
data/paper_universe.json
data/paper_liquidity_partial.json

# The expensive artefact of a full study — tens of MB of raw candidates, kept so
# re-analysis does not need another replay. Reproducible from tools/full_study.py.
reports/FULL-STUDY-candidates.json
